DATA SOURCES
------------
NOAA Space Weather Prediction Center (SWPC), https://www.swpc.noaa.gov/
  Kp index and forecast, F10.7 solar flux, sunspot predictions, solar wind,
  Dst and alerts. US Government work, public domain.

HamQSL solar data by Paul Herrman N0NBH, https://www.hamqsl.com/
  Supplementary band condition data (solarxml.php).

PSKReporter by Philip Gladstone N1DQ, https://pskreporter.info/
  Live FT8/FT4/WSPR reception reports. OrbitRx polls no more often than every
  5 minutes, as requested by the service, and identifies itself with an
  OrbitRx User-Agent.

DX cluster nodes (default: VE7CC, NC7J), operated by their respective sysops.

QRZ.com XML API (optional, needs the user's own subscription and key).

Contest Calendar by WA7BNM, https://www.contestcalendar.com/

ipinfo.io (optional, OFF by default). Only used when the user turns on
  "Look up my approximate location from my IP address". See PRIVACY.md.

MAPS AND LIBRARIES
------------------
The app loads only basemap/ne_110m_dark.png, a plate-carrée render of
  Natural Earth 1:110m land (public domain; third_party/natural_earth).
  world_map.jpg and the v2 PNG/WebP remain in git history and are not
  searched and not packaged. The 5 Nov 2026 exe was built before this and
  still contains the JPEG; this tree does not replace that file.
  The map is drawn natively with Qt (no embedded browser). It does not
  request a tile server. See README "Map image" and docs/MAP_IMAGE.md.

Ported code: the live spots, analytics, watchlist, rotor and OmniRig modules
in orbitrx/spots/ come from the author's earlier project "WSPR / FT8 Global
Matrix" (same author, relicensed here under MIT).

Python dependencies, from the upstream licence files for the versions
installed by Actions run 42004653668 (not from PyPI classifiers alone).
Details and the files that were read are in docs/DEPENDENCY_LICENCES.md.
  PySide6 6.12.0 / Qt: LicenseRef-Qt-Commercial OR LGPL-3.0-only OR GPL-2.0-only OR GPL-3.0-only (qtbase v6.12.0 qtcoreglobal.h).
  Pillow 13.0.0: MIT-CMU (Pillow LICENSE).
  matplotlib 3.11.2: the Matplotlib licence agreement, not the PSF licence.
  pyserial 3.5: BSD-3-Clause (LICENSE.txt).
  pywin32 b312: BSD-3-Clause in third_party/pywin32/License.txt (Mark Hammond). Not PSF.
    Verified in this tree: orbitrx/spots/omnirig.py imports win32com.client.
    orbitrx/alerts.py imports win10toast, not pywin32.
  win10toast 0.9: exact MIT text in third_party/win10toast/LICENSE, from
    repository commit 76d491638b (2017-07-21). The 0.9 wheel has no licence
    file and its METADATA says BSD. alerts.py imports it.
  PyInstaller 6.22.3 bootloader: third_party/pyinstaller/COPYING.txt
    (GPL-2.0-or-later plus the Bootloader Exception). The bootloader is
    embedded in the exe. Copying that file is not a grant for OrbitRx.
  Qt: the private prospective packaging route is LGPL-3.0-only for the Qt
    libraries, one alternative in the qtcoreglobal.h SPDX line. That is not
    clearance, not a published source offer, and not a commercial grant.
    The wheel's LicenseRef-Qt-Commercial pointer is not copied. As of
    2026-11-12 (F1), the Qt libraries actually linked and shipped are
    Qt6Core, Qt6Gui, Qt6Widgets, Qt6Network and Qt6Svg, together with
